# server/src/scripts/migrate.ts checksums each migration by hashing the bytes it reads
# off disk, and refuses to run when an already-applied file hashes differently — the
# check that catches a migration being edited after the fact.
#
# core.autocrlf is true here, so without this line a fresh clone would check the .sql
# files out as CRLF, all eleven applied migrations would hash differently, and the runner
# would hard-fail with "the database no longer matches the files" over line endings
# alone. Pinning them to LF makes the checksum mean what it is supposed to mean: the
# content changed, not the checkout did.
*.sql text eol=lf
